</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The first of the two cases was already proved by Braden and Vysogorets and appears as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, Equation (12)]</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We focus on the second case. Let us denote <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}=F\smallsetminus i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}=F\smallsetminus i</annotation></semantics></math>. We are assuming that <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a flat of <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using the definition of <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we analyze the possible values of <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\subseteq F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\subseteq F</annotation></semantics></math> a flat of <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\subseteq F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\subseteq F</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\notin G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\notin G</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\subseteq F_{0}\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\subseteq F_{0}\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\notin G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\notin G</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is also a flat of <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})=\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})=\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\subseteq F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\subseteq F</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in G</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{0}=G\smallsetminus i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{0}=G\smallsetminus i</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{0}\subseteq F_{0}\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{0}\subseteq F_{0}\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{0}=G\cap F_{0}\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{0}=G\cap F_{0}\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})=x^{-1}\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})=x^{-1}\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">We apply these in the following computation of <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}}^{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>F</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}}^{F})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
