<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}G_{0}\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\\
G_{0}\subseteq F_{0}\end{subarray}}x^{\rk(F)-\rk(G_{0}\cup\{i\})}P_{\mathsf{M}|_{F}/(G_{0}\cup\{i\})}(x^{-2})\cdot(x^{-1}\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G_{0}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}G_{0}\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\\
G_{0}\subseteq F_{0}\end{subarray}}x^{\rk(F)-\rk(G_{0}\cup\{i\})}P_{\mathsf{M}|_{F}/(G_{0}\cup\{i\})}(x^{-2})\cdot(x^{-1}\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G_{0}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">In the last equation, every appearance of the rank function is as the rank function of <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can relate this to the rank function of <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rk_{\mathsf{M}}(F)=\rk_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(F_{0})+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>rk</mi><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>rk</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rk_{\mathsf{M}}(F)=\rk_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(F_{0})+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\subseteq F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\subseteq F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rk_{\mathsf{M}}(G)=\rk_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>rk</mi><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>rk</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rk_{\mathsf{M}}(G)=\rk_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(G)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{0}\subseteq F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{0}\subseteq F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rk_{\mathsf{M}}(G_{0}\cup\{i\})=\rk_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(G_{0})+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>rk</mi><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>rk</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rk_{\mathsf{M}}(G_{0}\cup\{i\})=\rk_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(G_{0})+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">We also have Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomial identities under these conditions:</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the case in which <math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\subseteq F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\subseteq F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have an isomorphism <math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}|_{F}/G\cong(\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)|_{F_{0}}/G\oplus\mathsf{U}_{1,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}|_{F}/G\cong(\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)|_{F_{0}}/G\oplus\mathsf{U}_{1,1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore we obtain <math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathsf{M}|_{F}/G}(x^{-2})=P_{(\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)|_{F_{0}}/G}(x^{-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathsf{M}|_{F}/G}(x^{-2})=P_{(\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)|_{F_{0}}/G}(x^{-2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the case in which <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{0}\subseteq F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{0}\subseteq F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have an isomorphism <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}|_{F}/(G_{0}\cup\{i\})\cong(\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)|_{F_{0}}/{G_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}|_{F}/(G_{0}\cup\{i\})\cong(\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)|_{F_{0}}/{G_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathsf{M}|_{F}/(G_{0}\cup\{i\})}(x^{-2})=P_{(\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)|_{F_{0}}/G_{0}}(x^{-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathsf{M}|_{F}/(G_{0}\cup\{i\})}(x^{-2})=P_{(\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)|_{F_{0}}/G_{0}}(x^{-2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting these identities into the two summands in equation (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.2. A homomorphism for single element deletions ‣ 3. Proof of the deletion formulas ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), we have</span></p>
