<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3. </span>The deletion formula for inverse KL polynomials</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have all the necessary ingredients to prove the first part of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 1.4 ‣ 1.1. Main results ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthmintro1x1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thmintro1">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthmintro1x1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem </span><a href="#S1.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 1.4 ‣ 1.1. Main results ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a><span id="Thmthmintro1x1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (first part)</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmthmintro1x1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthmintro1x1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmthmintro1x1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> be a loopless matroid on <math id="Thmthmintro1x1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="Thmthmintro1x1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in E</annotation></semantics></math> be an element that is not a coloop. The following identity holds:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=Q_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(x)+(1+x)Q_{\mathsf{M}/i}(x)-\sum_{F\in\mathcal{T}_{i}}\uptau(\mathsf{M}|_{F}/i)\,x^{\rk(F)/2}\,Q_{\mathsf{M}/F}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\uptau</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=Q_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(x)+(1+x)Q_{\mathsf{M}/i}(x)-\sum_{F\in\mathcal{T}_{i}}\uptau(\mathsf{M}|_{F}/i)\,x^{\rk(F)/2}\,Q_{\mathsf{M}/F}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We use Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 3.2 ‣ 3.1. The Kazhdan–Lusztig basis ‣ 3. Proof of the deletion formulas ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> for <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=E</annotation></semantics></math> the full ground set, and obtain</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{E}=\sum_{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}x^{\rk(E)-\rk(G)}\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}/G}(x^{-2})\,\upzeta^{G}_{\mathsf{M}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{E}=\sum_{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}x^{\rk(E)-\rk(G)}\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}/G}(x^{-2})\,\upzeta^{G}_{\mathsf{M}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the homomorphism <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{E\smallsetminus i}=\sum_{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}x^{\rk(E)-\rk(G)}\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}/G}(x^{-2})\cdot\Delta(\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{E\smallsetminus i}=\sum_{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}x^{\rk(E)-\rk(G)}\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}/G}(x^{-2})\cdot\Delta(\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}}^{G}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">By writing both sides of equation (<a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.3. The deletion formula for inverse KL polynomials ‣ 3. Proof of the deletion formulas ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) in the Kazhdan–Lusztig basis, we may equate the resulting coefficients of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math>. On the left-hand side we apply Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 3.2 ‣ 3.1. The Kazhdan–Lusztig basis ‣ 3. Proof of the deletion formulas ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> again, but now for the matroid <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i</annotation></semantics></math> and the flat <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\smallsetminus i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\smallsetminus i</annotation></semantics></math>. We obtain that the coefficient of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math> on the left-hand side equals
<math id="S3.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\rk_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(E\smallsetminus i)-\rk_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(\varnothing)}\cdot\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}|_{E\smallsetminus i}}(x^{-2})=x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})}\cdot\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(x^{-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>rk</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>rk</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\rk_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(E\smallsetminus i)-\rk_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(\varnothing)}\cdot\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}|_{E\smallsetminus i}}(x^{-2})=x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})}\cdot\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(x^{-2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">To compute the coefficient of <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upzeta^{\varnothing}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upzeta^{\varnothing}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}</annotation></semantics></math> on the right-hand side of equation (<a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.3. The deletion formula for inverse KL polynomials ‣ 3. Proof of the deletion formulas ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>), we employ Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3.3 ‣ 3.2. A homomorphism for single element deletions ‣ 3. Proof of the deletion formulas ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>. Examining the summand for <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in{L}(\mathsf{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in{L}(\mathsf{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, this coefficient is non-zero only when <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in\{\varnothing,i\}\cup{T}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in\{\varnothing,i\}\cup{T}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. In each of these cases, we have the following:</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}}^{\varnothing})=\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}}^{\varnothing})=\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=i</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}}^{i})=(x+x^{-1})\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}}^{i})=(x+x^{-1})\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in{T}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in{T}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.I5.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})=\uptau(\mathsf{M}|_{G}/i)\cdot\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}+(\text{terms not including $\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}$})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\uptau</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>terms not including </mtext><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})=\uptau(\mathsf{M}|_{G}/i)\cdot\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}+(\text{terms not including $\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}$})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Collecting all these terms, the coefficient of <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math> on the right-hand side of equation (<a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.3. The deletion formula for inverse KL polynomials ‣ 3. Proof of the deletion formulas ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) equals</span></p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})}\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}}(x^{-2})+x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})-1}(x+x^{-1})\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}/i}(x^{-2})+\sum_{G\in{T}_{i}}x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})-\rk(G)}\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}/G}(x^{-2})\cdot\uptau(\mathsf{M}|_{G}/i)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext class="undefined">\uptau</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})}\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}}(x^{-2})+x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})-1}(x+x^{-1})\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}/i}(x^{-2})+\sum_{G\in{T}_{i}}x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})-\rk(G)}\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}/G}(x^{-2})\cdot\uptau(\mathsf{M}|_{G}/i).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now, our result follows by equating this with the computation we made of this coefficient on the left-hand side of equation (<a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.3. The deletion formula for inverse KL polynomials ‣ 3. Proof of the deletion formulas ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})}\cdot\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(x^{-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})}\cdot\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(x^{-2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})}\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}}(x^{-2})+x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})-1}(x+x^{-1})\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}/i}(x^{-2})+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})}\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}}(x^{-2})+x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})-1}(x+x^{-1})\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}/i}(x^{-2})+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\sum_{G\in{T}_{i}}x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})-\rk(G)}\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}/G}(x^{-2})\cdot\uptau(\mathsf{M}|_{G}/i)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext class="undefined">\uptau</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\sum_{G\in{T}_{i}}x^{\rk(\mathsf{M})-\rk(G)}\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}/G}(x^{-2})\cdot\uptau(\mathsf{M}|_{G}/i).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">By rearranging terms, applying the substitution <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=(-1)^{\rk(\mathsf{M})}Q_{\mathsf{M}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=(-1)^{\rk(\mathsf{M})}Q_{\mathsf{M}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and using the change of variables <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{-2}=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{-2}=t</annotation></semantics></math>, we are led to the formula we desired.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4. </span>Deletion formula for the inverse <math id="S3.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>-polynomial</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to prove the deletion formula for <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\mathsf{M}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\mathsf{M}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the related polynomial <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> given by</p>
<table id="S3.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}}(x):=(-1)^{\rk(\mathsf{M})}\,Y_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=\sum_{F\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}\left(x^{\rk(\mathsf{M}/F)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/F)\right)\cdot\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}|_{F}}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}}(x):=(-1)^{\rk(\mathsf{M})}\,Y_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=\sum_{F\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}\left(x^{\rk(\mathsf{M}/F)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/F)\right)\cdot\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}|_{F}}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We define a new family of elements in <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(\mathsf{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(\mathsf{M})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{F}:=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\\
G\subseteq F\end{subarray}}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}|_{F}/G)\,\cdot\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>F</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.225em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{F}:=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\\
G\subseteq F\end{subarray}}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}|_{F}/G)\,\cdot\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Because the Möbius invariant of the rank zero matroid is <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, these elements form a new <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}[x,x^{-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}[x,x^{-1}]</annotation></semantics></math>-basis of
<math id="S3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(\mathsf{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(\mathsf{M})</annotation></semantics></math>. The next lemma shows how the deletion map <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> interacts with these elements.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.4</span></span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> be a matroid on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in E</annotation></semantics></math> be an element of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I6" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S3.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S3.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I6.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a coloop of </span><math id="S3.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I6.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="S3.I6.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E})=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I6.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S3.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S3.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I6.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is not a coloop of </span><math id="S3.I6.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I6.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="S3.I6.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E})=\upxi_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{E\smallsetminus i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E})=\upxi_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{E\smallsetminus i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I6.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}[x,x^{-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}[x,x^{-1}]</annotation></semantics></math>-linear, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E})=\sum_{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E})=\sum_{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">We partition the lattice of flats <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})</annotation></semantics></math> into four disjoint sets:</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M}):i\notin G\text{ and }G\cup i\notin\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M}):i\notin G\text{ and }G\cup i\notin\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M}):i\notin G\text{ and }G\cup i\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M}):i\notin G\text{ and }G\cup i\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I7.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M}):i\in G\text{ and }G\smallsetminus i\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M}):i\in G\text{ and }G\smallsetminus i\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I7.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I7.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I7.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I7.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M}):i\in G\text{ and }G\smallsetminus i\notin\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M}):i\in G\text{ and }G\smallsetminus i\notin\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">We can now rewrite the sum by splitting it over these four sets:</span></p>
<table id="S3.SS4.p3.4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\upxi^{E}_{\mathsf{M}})=\sum_{G\in S}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})+\sum_{G\in T}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})\\
\qquad+\sum_{G\in A}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})+\sum_{G\in B}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\upxi^{E}_{\mathsf{M}})=\sum_{G\in S}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})+\sum_{G\in T}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})\\
\qquad+\sum_{G\in A}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})+\sum_{G\in B}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the definition of <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> to each sum, one obtains:</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I8" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.I8.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in S\cup A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in S\cup A</annotation></semantics></math> (flats not containing <math id="S3.I8.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>), we have <math id="S3.I8.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})=\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G\smallsetminus i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})=\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G\smallsetminus i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.I8.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in T</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.I8.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})=x^{-1}\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G\smallsetminus i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})=x^{-1}\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G\smallsetminus i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I8.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I8.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I8.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.I8.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in B</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.I8.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})=\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G\smallsetminus i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})=\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G\smallsetminus i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting these into the expression above gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.SS4.p3.7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\upxi^{E}_{\mathsf{M}})=\sum_{G\in S}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Gamma^{G}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}+\sum_{G\in T}x^{\rk(G)-1}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G\smallsetminus i}\\
+\sum_{G\in A}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Gamma^{G}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}+\sum_{G\in B}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G\smallsetminus i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\upxi^{E}_{\mathsf{M}})=\sum_{G\in S}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Gamma^{G}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}+\sum_{G\in T}x^{\rk(G)-1}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G\smallsetminus i}\\
+\sum_{G\in A}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Gamma^{G}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}+\sum_{G\in B}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G\smallsetminus i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text">There is a natural bijection between <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> where for each <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\cup i\in T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\cup i\in T</annotation></semantics></math>. We re-index the sum over <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, which lets us combine the first two sums:</span></p>
<table id="S3.SS4.p3.9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.SS4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\upxi^{E}_{\mathsf{M}})=\sum_{F\in S}\left(x^{\rk(F)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/F)+x^{\rk(F\cup i)-1}\mu(\mathsf{M}/(F\cup i))\right)\cdot\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{F}\\
+\sum_{G\in A}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Gamma^{G}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}+\sum_{G\in B}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G\smallsetminus i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>F</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\upxi^{E}_{\mathsf{M}})=\sum_{F\in S}\left(x^{\rk(F)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/F)+x^{\rk(F\cup i)-1}\mu(\mathsf{M}/(F\cup i))\right)\cdot\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{F}\\
+\sum_{G\in A}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Gamma^{G}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}+\sum_{G\in B}x^{\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)\cdot\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G\smallsetminus i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p3.10.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, note that <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rk(F\cup i)=\rk(F)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rk(F\cup i)=\rk(F)+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We note that in the case where <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is a coloop of <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, the sets <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> are empty. We also have that <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is a coloop in the contraction <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}/F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}/F</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in S</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\mathsf{M}/F)=-\mu(\mathsf{M}/(F\cup i))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\mathsf{M}/F)=-\mu(\mathsf{M}/(F\cup i))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E})</annotation></semantics></math> simplifies to <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, proving the statement (<a href="#S3.I6.i1" title="Item i ‣ Lemma 3.4 ‣ 3.4. Deletion formula for the inverse 𝑍-polynomial ‣ 3. Proof of the deletion formulas ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">i</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">In the case where <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is not a coloop of <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is neither a loop nor a coloop of the contraction <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}/F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}/F</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the standard deletion-contraction relation for the Möbius function:</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\mathsf{M}/F)+\mu(\mathsf{M}/(F\cup i))=\mu((\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)/F)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\mathsf{M}/F)+\mu(\mathsf{M}/(F\cup i))=\mu((\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)/F).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">There are analogous relations for the flats in the other sets. For a flat <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in A</annotation></semantics></math>, the interval <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[G,E]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[G,E]</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})</annotation></semantics></math> is isomorphic to the interval <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[G,E\smallsetminus i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[G,E\smallsetminus i]</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)</annotation></semantics></math>, which gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)=\mu((\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)/G)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)=\mu((\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)/G).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">For a flat <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in B</annotation></semantics></math>, the set <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=G\smallsetminus i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=G\smallsetminus i</annotation></semantics></math> is a flat in <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i</annotation></semantics></math> but not in <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The intervals <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[G,E]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[G,E]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[G\smallsetminus i,E\smallsetminus i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[G\smallsetminus i,E\smallsetminus i]</annotation></semantics></math> are isomorphic, so the relationship between the Möbius functions in this case is</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)=\mu((\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)/(G\smallsetminus i))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\mathsf{M}/G)=\mu((\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)/(G\smallsetminus i)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting these identities into the expression for <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\upxi^{E}_{\mathsf{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\upxi^{E}_{\mathsf{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="S3.SS4.p5.5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.SS4.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E})=\sum_{F\in S}x^{\rk(F)}\mu((\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)/F)\cdot\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{F}+\sum_{G\in A}x^{\rk(G)}\mu((\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)/G)\cdot\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G}\\
+\sum_{G\in B}x^{\rk(G)}\mu((\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)/(G\smallsetminus i))\cdot\Gamma^{G\smallsetminus i}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>F</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E})=\sum_{F\in S}x^{\rk(F)}\mu((\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)/F)\cdot\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{F}+\sum_{G\in A}x^{\rk(G)}\mu((\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)/G)\cdot\Gamma_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{G}\\
+\sum_{G\in B}x^{\rk(G)}\mu((\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i)/(G\smallsetminus i))\cdot\Gamma^{G\smallsetminus i}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">Since the terms on the right account exactly for all flats of the matroid <math id="S3.SS4.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E})=\upxi_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{E\smallsetminus i}.\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E})=\upxi_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{E\smallsetminus i}.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We are now ready to prove the second part of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 1.4 ‣ 1.1. Main results ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthmintro2x1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thmintro2">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthmintro2x1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem </span><a href="#S1.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 1.4 ‣ 1.1. Main results ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a><span id="Thmthmintro2x1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (second part)</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmthmintro2x1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthmintro2x1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmthmintro2x1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> be a loopless matroid on <math id="Thmthmintro2x1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="Thmthmintro2x1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in E</annotation></semantics></math> be an element that is not a coloop. The following identity holds:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=Y_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(x)+(1+x)Y_{\mathsf{M}/i}(x)-\sum_{F\in\mathcal{T}_{i}}\uptau(\mathsf{M}|_{F}/i)\,x^{\rk(F)/2}\,Y_{\mathsf{M}/F}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\uptau</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=Y_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(x)+(1+x)Y_{\mathsf{M}/i}(x)-\sum_{F\in\mathcal{T}_{i}}\uptau(\mathsf{M}|_{F}/i)\,x^{\rk(F)/2}\,Y_{\mathsf{M}/F}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By applying Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 3.2 ‣ 3.1. The Kazhdan–Lusztig basis ‣ 3. Proof of the deletion formulas ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> to the definition of the element <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upxi^{E}_{\mathsf{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upxi^{E}_{\mathsf{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write it in terms of the Kazhdan–Lusztig basis elements:</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{F\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}x^{\rk(F)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/F)\left(\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\\
G\subseteq F\end{subarray}}x^{\rk(F)-\rk(G)}\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}|_{F}/G}(x^{-2})\cdot\upzeta^{G}_{\mathsf{M}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{F\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}x^{\rk(F)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/F)\left(\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\\
G\subseteq F\end{subarray}}x^{\rk(F)-\rk(G)}\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}|_{F}/G}(x^{-2})\cdot\upzeta^{G}_{\mathsf{M}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{F\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\\
G\subseteq F\end{subarray}}x^{2\rk(F)-\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/F)\cdot\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}|_{F}/G}(x^{-2})\cdot\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{F\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\\
G\subseteq F\end{subarray}}x^{2\rk(F)-\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/F)\cdot\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}|_{F}/G}(x^{-2})\cdot\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}F\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\\
F\supseteq G\end{subarray}}x^{2\rk(F)-\rk(G)}\mu(\mathsf{M}/F)\cdot\widehat{Q}_{\mathsf{M}|_{F}/G}(x^{-2})\cdot\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⊇</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}F\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})\\
