<p id="S3.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the deletion map <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> to this expression and using Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 3.4 ‣ 3.4. Deletion formula for the inverse 𝑍-polynomial ‣ 3. Proof of the deletion formulas ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, we get</span></p>
<table id="S3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upxi_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{E\smallsetminus i}=\Delta(\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E})=\sum_{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}x^{2\rk(E)-\rk(G)}\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}/G}(x^{-2})\cdot\Delta(\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}}^{G})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upxi</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mi>𝖬</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upxi_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{E\smallsetminus i}=\Delta(\upxi_{\mathsf{M}}^{E})=\sum_{G\in\mathcal{L}(\mathsf{M})}x^{2\rk(E)-\rk(G)}\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}/G}(x^{-2})\cdot\Delta(\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}}^{G}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">By applying equation (<a href="#S3.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.4. Deletion formula for the inverse 𝑍-polynomial ‣ 3. Proof of the deletion formulas ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) to the matroid <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i</annotation></semantics></math> with ground set <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\smallsetminus i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\smallsetminus i</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain that the coefficient of <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math> on the left-hand side of equation (<a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.4. Deletion formula for the inverse 𝑍-polynomial ‣ 3. Proof of the deletion formulas ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) equals <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2\rk(E\smallsetminus i)}\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(x^{-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2\rk(E\smallsetminus i)}\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(x^{-2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Like in the proof of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 1.4 ‣ 1.1. Main results ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a> (first part), the coefficient of <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math> on the right-hand side of equation (<a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.4. Deletion formula for the inverse 𝑍-polynomial ‣ 3. Proof of the deletion formulas ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) is</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2\rk(E)}\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}}(x^{-2})-(x+x^{-1})x^{2\rk(E)-1}\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}/i}(x^{-2})+\sum_{G\in{T}_{i}}\uptau(\mathsf{M}|_{G}/i)\cdot x^{2\rk(E)-\rk(G)}\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}/G}(x^{-2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\uptau</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2\rk(E)}\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}}(x^{-2})-(x+x^{-1})x^{2\rk(E)-1}\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}/i}(x^{-2})+\sum_{G\in{T}_{i}}\uptau(\mathsf{M}|_{G}/i)\cdot x^{2\rk(E)-\rk(G)}\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}/G}(x^{-2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Equating the coefficients of <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mtext class="undefined">\upzeta</mtext><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upzeta_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}^{\varnothing}</annotation></semantics></math> on both sides, we get</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(x^{-2})=\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}}(x^{-2})-(1+x^{-2})\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}/i}(x^{-2})+\sum_{G\in{T}_{i}}\uptau(\mathsf{M}|_{G}/i)\cdot x^{-\rk(G)}\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}/G}(x^{-2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\uptau</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}\smallsetminus i}(x^{-2})=\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}}(x^{-2})-(1+x^{-2})\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}/i}(x^{-2})+\sum_{G\in{T}_{i}}\uptau(\mathsf{M}|_{G}/i)\cdot x^{-\rk(G)}\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}/G}(x^{-2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">After applying the change of variables <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=x^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=x^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, rearranging terms, and using that <math id="S3.SS4.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=(-1)^{\rk(\mathsf{M})}Y_{\mathsf{M}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Y}_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=(-1)^{\rk(\mathsf{M})}Y_{\mathsf{M}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, the desired deletion formula follows.
∎</span></p>
