<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4. </span>Some special cases and examples</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to illustrate its use, in this section we apply Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 1.4 ‣ 1.1. Main results ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a> to a few special cases.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1. </span>Uniform matroids</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following is a new recursion that allows for the computation of inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig and inverse <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>-polynomials of uniform matroids.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.1</span></span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}=\mathsf{U}_{k,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}=\mathsf{U}_{k,n}</annotation></semantics></math> be a uniform matroid of rank <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> elements, where <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;k&lt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;k&lt;n</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Q_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n-1}}(x)+(1+x)\cdot Q_{\mathsf{U}_{k-1,n-1}}(x)-\uptau(\mathsf{U}_{k-1,n-1})\cdot x^{k/2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\uptau</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Q_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n-1}}(x)+(1+x)\cdot Q_{\mathsf{U}_{k-1,n-1}}(x)-\uptau(\mathsf{U}_{k-1,n-1})\cdot x^{k/2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Y_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n-1}}(x)+(1+x)\cdot Y_{\mathsf{U}_{k-1,n-1}}(x)-\uptau(\mathsf{U}_{k-1,n-1})\cdot x^{k/2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\uptau</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Y_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n-1}}(x)+(1+x)\cdot Y_{\mathsf{U}_{k-1,n-1}}(x)-\uptau(\mathsf{U}_{k-1,n-1})\cdot x^{k/2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
