</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;n</annotation></semantics></math>, none of the elements in the ground set are coloops; thus, we may apply the deletion formula for a generic element <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in the ground set. The set <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{T}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{T}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> then consists only of the top flat <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, and the sum over <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{T}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{T}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> reduces exactly to the sum in our statement.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The reader may compare the above identities with the following formulas for <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, Theorem 3.3]</cite>, and for <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, Theorem 1.1]</cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\binom{n}{k}\sum_{j=0}^{\lfloor\frac{k-1}{2}\rfloor}\frac{(n-k)(k-2j)}{(n-k+j)(n-j)}\binom{k}{j}\,x^{j}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\binom{n}{k}\sum_{j=0}^{\lfloor\frac{k-1}{2}\rfloor}\frac{(n-k)(k-2j)}{(n-k+j)(n-j)}\binom{k}{j}\,x^{j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{\mathsf{U}_{k,n}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=0}^{\lfloor\frac{k}{2}\rfloor}\binom{n}{i}\binom{n-i-1}{n-k}\,x^{i}+\sum_{i=0}^{\lfloor\frac{k-1}{2}\rfloor}\binom{n}{i}\binom{n-i-1}{n-k}\,x^{k-i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=0}^{\lfloor\frac{k}{2}\rfloor}\binom{n}{i}\binom{n-i-1}{n-k}\,x^{i}+\sum_{i=0}^{\lfloor\frac{k-1}{2}\rfloor}\binom{n}{i}\binom{n-i-1}{n-k}\,x^{k-i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The first of the above two formulas, along with a result due to Vecchi in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, Theorem 4.1]</cite>, implies that</p>
<table id="S4.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uptau(\mathsf{U}_{k,n})=\begin{cases}\displaystyle\binom{n}{k}\binom{k}{\lfloor\frac{k-1}{2}\rfloor}\dfrac{4(n-k)}{(2n-k-1)(2n-k+1)}&amp;\text{if $k$ is odd,}\\
0&amp;\text{if $k$ is even.}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\uptau</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mi>k</mi><mtext> is odd,</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mi>k</mi><mtext> is even.</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uptau(\mathsf{U}_{k,n})=\begin{cases}\displaystyle\binom{n}{k}\binom{k}{\lfloor\frac{k-1}{2}\rfloor}\dfrac{4(n-k)}{(2n-k-1)(2n-k+1)}&amp;\text{if $k$ is odd,}\\
0&amp;\text{if $k$ is even.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
