<p id="S4.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this back into the general formula from Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 1.4 ‣ 1.1. Main results ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a>, and using the fact that the contraction <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}/i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖬</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}/i</annotation></semantics></math> is isomorphic to <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{PG}(r-2,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>PG</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{PG}(r-2,q)</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</span></p>
