<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>A counterexample to Conjecture <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem3" title="Conjecture 1.3 ([, Conjecture 1.4]) ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.3</span></a></h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> be a matroid of rank <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> without loops. The lattice of flats of <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> has the empty set as its bottom element and <math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> as its top element. This guarantees that the rank <math id="S5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> flats of <math id="S5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> form a partition of <math id="S5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>. Conversely, any partition of <math id="S5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> yields a loopless rank <math id="S5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> matroid on <math id="S5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By taking duals, the above construction yields a procedure that builds a corank <math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> matroid on <math id="S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> without coloops from every set partition of <math id="S5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 5.1</span></span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=8</annotation></semantics></math> and the partition of the set <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\ldots,8\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\ldots,8\}</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of the parts <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,5,6,8\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,5,6,8\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{2\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{3,4,7\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{3,4,7\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The loopless rank <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> matroid that has these three sets as its rank <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> flats is the graphic matroid induced by the graph depicted in Figure <a href="#S5.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Example 5.1 ‣ 5. A counterexample to Conjecture ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. (If there are more than three parts in the partition, these matroids fail to be graphic.) The corank <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> matroid associated to this set partition is the corresponding matroid dual.</p>
</div>
