<div id="S5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By a direct application of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, Theorem 5.3]</cite>, we obtain that for any coloopless corank <math id="S5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> matroid on <math id="S5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> elements, the following equality holds:</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=Q_{\mathsf{U}_{n-2,n}}(x)-\sum_{r,h}\uplambda_{r,h}\left(Q_{\mathsf{\Lambda}_{r,n-2,h,n}}(x)-Q_{\mathsf{U}_{n-2-r,n-h}}(x)Q_{\mathsf{U}_{r,h}}(x)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mtext class="undefined">\uplambda</mtext><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Λ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=Q_{\mathsf{U}_{n-2,n}}(x)-\sum_{r,h}\uplambda_{r,h}\left(Q_{\mathsf{\Lambda}_{r,n-2,h,n}}(x)-Q_{\mathsf{U}_{n-2-r,n-h}}(x)Q_{\mathsf{U}_{r,h}}(x)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uplambda_{r,h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="undefined">\uplambda</mtext><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uplambda_{r,h}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of stressed subsets of <math id="S5.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> that have rank <math id="S5.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and size <math id="S5.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. (We omit the definition of the matroid <math id="S5.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Lambda}_{r,n-2,h,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Λ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Lambda}_{r,n-2,h,n}</annotation></semantics></math> because it is inessential for this proof, as we will see in what follows.)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> has corank <math id="S5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, the definition of being a stressed subset implies that <math id="S5.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\{r,r+1,r+2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\{r,r+1,r+2\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and in fact the cases <math id="S5.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=r+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=r+2</annotation></semantics></math> cannot happen. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=Q_{\mathsf{U}_{n-2,n}}(x)-\sum_{r}\uplambda_{r}\left(Q_{\mathsf{\Lambda}_{r,n-2,r+1,n}}(x)-Q_{\mathsf{U}_{n-r-2,n-r-1}}(x)Q_{\mathsf{U}_{r,r+1}}(x)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>r</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mtext class="undefined">\uplambda</mtext><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Λ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=Q_{\mathsf{U}_{n-2,n}}(x)-\sum_{r}\uplambda_{r}\left(Q_{\mathsf{\Lambda}_{r,n-2,r+1,n}}(x)-Q_{\mathsf{U}_{n-r-2,n-r-1}}(x)Q_{\mathsf{U}_{r,r+1}}(x)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where now <math id="S5.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uplambda_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="undefined">\uplambda</mtext><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uplambda_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> counts the number of stressed subsets of rank <math id="S5.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and size <math id="S5.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r+1</annotation></semantics></math>. By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, Corollary 5.7]</cite>, since the inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomial is a valuative invariant, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
