</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p8.1" class="ltx_p">With this formula at hand, it is straightforward to compute <math id="S5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathsf{M}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathsf{M}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\mathsf{M}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\mathsf{M}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for very large matroids <math id="S5.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> of corank <math id="S5.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. For all such matroids, up to cardinality <math id="S5.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math>, Conjecture <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem3" title="Conjecture 1.3 ([, Conjecture 1.4]) ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.3</span></a> is true. However, starting at <math id="S5.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="21" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>21</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">21</annotation></semantics></math> elements counterexamples appear. The following result implies Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 1.5 ‣ 1.1. Main results ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5.3</span></span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The corank <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> matroid induced by partitioning the set <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\ldots,21\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>21</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\ldots,21\}</annotation></semantics></math> into six parts of sizes <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(4,4,4,3,3,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(4,4,4,3,3,3)</annotation></semantics></math> is a counterexample to Conjecture <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem3" title="Conjecture 1.3 ([, Conjecture 1.4]) ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomialsof matroids under deletion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.3</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Computing the inverse Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomial via the preceding theorem results in</span></p>
<table id="S5.p9.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=71162\,x^{9}+232662\,x^{8}+350404\,x^{7}+323646\,x^{6}\\
+215169\,x^{5}+106659\,x^{4}+39217\,x^{3}+10323\,x^{2}+1790\,x+163." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>71162</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>9</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>232662</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>350404</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>323646</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>215169</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>106659</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>39217</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>10323</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1790</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>163</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathsf{M}}(x)=71162\,x^{9}+232662\,x^{8}+350404\,x^{7}+323646\,x^{6}\\
+215169\,x^{5}+106659\,x^{4}+39217\,x^{3}+10323\,x^{2}+1790\,x+163.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">After normalizing, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S5.p9.4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}(Q_{\mathsf{M}})(x)=71162\,x^{9}+2093958\,x^{8}+12614544\,x^{7}+27186264\,x^{6}\\
+27111294\,x^{5}+13439034\,x^{4}+3294228\,x^{3}+371628\,x^{2}+16110\,x+163." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>𝖬</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>71162</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>9</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2093958</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>12614544</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>27186264</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>27111294</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>13439034</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3294228</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>371628</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16110</mn><mo lspace="0.340em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>163</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}(Q_{\mathsf{M}})(x)=71162\,x^{9}+2093958\,x^{8}+12614544\,x^{7}+27186264\,x^{6}\\
+27111294\,x^{5}+13439034\,x^{4}+3294228\,x^{3}+371628\,x^{2}+16110\,x+163.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
